# Theme Feature

## Architecture

Dark mode is implemented via a React context in `client/components/theme/ThemeContext.tsx`.

- **Provider**: `ThemeProvider` — wrap at the root of `App.tsx` (outside `AuthProvider`)
- **Hook**: `useTheme()` — returns `{ isDark: boolean, toggleDark: () => void }`

## Initialization order (on mount)

1. Check `localStorage.getItem("theme")` — `"dark"` or `"light"` wins
2. Fall back to `window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches`

## Persistence

User choice is stored in `localStorage` under the key `"theme"` (values: `"dark"` | `"light"`).

## DOM mechanism

When `isDark` changes, the effect adds or removes the `.dark` class on `document.documentElement`. Tailwind's `darkMode: ["class"]` config picks this up automatically.

## CSS tokens

Light tokens live in `:root`, dark overrides live in `.dark` — both in `client/global.css`. The `.dark` block includes surface-container variants (`-low`, default, `-high`) so dropdowns and panels render correctly in dark mode.

## Toggle UI

The dark mode toggle is the first row inside the Settings dropdown in `client/components/calendar/TopBar.tsx`, using the same pill-button pattern as the 24-hour time and week-start toggles.
